   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><h1 style=\"font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:22px;line-height:1.3;font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(36,39,41)\"><div style=\"padding-right:15px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:top;box-sizing:inherit;width:auto\"><div style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;text-align:center;min-width:46px\"><span style=\"margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:8px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:20px;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;display:block;color:rgb(106,115,124)\"><br>1</span><a title=\"This question does not show any research effort; it is unclear or not useful\" style=\"margin-right:auto;margin-bottom:10px;margin-left:auto;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:1px;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(0,119,204);background-image:url(&quot;&quot;),none;background-size:initial;background-repeat:no-repeat;overflow:hidden;display:block;width:40px;min-height:30px;background-position:0px -220px\" rel=\"nofollow\">down vote</a><a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/49317059/how-to-save-the-values-of-the-factors-of-a-cfa-analysis-in-my-dataset#\" title=\"Click to mark as favorite question (click again to undo)\" style=\"margin-right:auto;margin-bottom:2px;margin-left:auto;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:1px;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(0,119,204);background-image:url(&quot;&quot;),none;background-size:initial;background-repeat:no-repeat;overflow:hidden;display:block;width:40px;min-height:30px;background-position:0px -120px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stackoverflow.com/questions/49317059/how-to-save-the-values-of-the-factors-of-a-cfa-analysis-in-my-dataset%23&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425935589000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1BEYVFIlMYI8wvAcA0lGdU\">favorite</a><div style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit\"><span style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;color:rgb(106,115,124)\"></span></div></div></div><div style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:top;box-sizing:inherit;width:auto;min-width:0px\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:15px;line-height:1.3;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;width:667px;word-wrap:break-word\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\">I performed a CFA using the lavaan package</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:13px;line-height:inherit;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);word-wrap:normal\"><code style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;white-space:inherit\">require(&#39;lavaan&#39;);\r\n\r\nHS.model &lt;- &#39;external_regulation_soc =~ JOBMOTIVATIE_extsoc1 + \r\n                  JOBMOTIVATIE_extsoc2 + JOBMOTIVATIE_extsoc3\r\n             external_regulation_mat =~ JOBMOTIVATIE_extmat1 + \r\n                  JOBMOTIVATIE_extmat2 + JOBMOTIVATIE_extmat3\r\n             introjected_regulation =~ JOBMOTIVATIE_introj1 + \r\n                  JOBMOTIVATIE_introj2 + JOBMOTIVATIE_introj3 + \r\n                  JOBMOTIVATIE_introj4\r\n             identified_regulation =~ JOBMOTIVATIE_ident1 + \r\n                  JOBMOTIVATIE_ident2 + JOBMOTIVATIE_ident3\r\n             intrinsic_motivation =~ JOBMOTIVATIE_intrin1 + \r\n                  JOBMOTIVATIE_intrin2 + JOBMOTIVATIE_intrin3&#39;\r\n\r\nfit &lt;- cfa(HS.model, data = dataset, scores=&quot;regression&quot;)\r\n\r\nsummary(fit, fit.measures=TRUE, standardized=TRUE)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\">I managed to get the values for the five factors in a seperate dataset using</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:13px;line-height:inherit;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);word-wrap:normal\"><code style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;white-space:inherit\">data_factor &lt;- predict(fit)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\">But I need these 5 factors (as columns, as variables), added to my original dataset. How can I achieve this?</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\">I tried cbind, but got an error:</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:13px;line-height:inherit;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);word-wrap:normal\"><code style=\"font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;white-space:inherit\">factorERS &lt;- select(dataset, JOBMOTIVATIE_extsoc1 + \r\n                   JOBMOTIVATIE_extsoc2 + JOBMOTIVATIE_extsoc3)\r\n\r\ndata_CFA &lt;- cbind(dataset, fit$scores)\r\nError in fit$scores : $ operator not defined for this S4 class\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both\">Thanks for helping me out!</p><div><br></div></div></div></h1></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "L4cq2oK9BAAJ",
   "from": "Christopher David Desjardins",
   "author": "189d19347ab44a74",
   "date": "2018-03-16T17:00:38Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to save the values of the factors of a CFA analysis in my dataset?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>Lies,<br><br></div><div>This works for me:<br><br>library(&quot;lavaan&quot;)<br>HS.model &lt;- &#39;<br>visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3<br>textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6<br>speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9<br>&#39;<br>fit &lt;- cfa(HS.model, data=HolzingerSwineford1939, scores = &quot;regression&quot;)<br>cbind(HolzingerSwineford1939, data.frame(predict(fit)))<br><br></div><div>How about for you:<br><br></div>data_CFA &lt;- cbind(dataset, data.frame(predict(fit)))<br><br><br></div><div>Chris<br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
